referenceAnswer.en:
Under noUncheckedIndexedAccess an index access widens to `T | undefined`, so `return arr[0];` fails with `error TS2322: Type 'T | undefined' is not assignable to type 'T'.` Fix: widen the signature, or narrow before returning.

```typescript
function getFirstElement<T>(arr: T[]): T | undefined {
  return arr[0];
}
```

